    {
      "id": "a871376bc5bed9e053e802032c22f076ac45e609",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2182105432,
          "type": null,
          "body": "None of the Wireshark executables currently use the GOption API, so this would only be useful for other programs linking with wsutil, correct? This isn't necessarily a blocker, just a point of clarification.",
          "author": {
            "id": 860017,
            "username": "geraldcombs",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Gerald Combs",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/860017/avatar.png?v=1788825804",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/geraldcombs"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-28T19:08:55.863Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-28T19:08:55.863Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 337083009,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17817,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5b77cfc132cd300010703d29d9afa6c56bef6089",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2182127413,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yes, that's correct, I should have clarified that. I think it could be interesting to use the GOption API for Wireshark but that is not something I am planning to work on, and it would probably raise some concerns over backward compatibility (and to be fair I think I remember finding some odd quirks with GOption in the past), so I would understand if this MR is not worthwhile.\n\nI think it could be useful for things like new unit test utilities that could adopt GOption as an alternative to `ws_getopt()` (which is how I am using it).",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-28T19:25:28.324Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-28T19:25:28.324Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 337083009,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 17817,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "be75ba98ae88a6289268197348150c0218d4f866",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2186039536,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I shouldn't say odd quirks, I think I hit a bug that I should have reported upstream when I tried to use GOption with dftest but didn't.\n\nMaybe it would be nice to use a higher level API for option parsing and remove some bundled code for ws_getopt().\n\nAnyway this isn't a very interesting MR to merge overall, I agree with that, so I'm closing it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-30T15:17:28.889Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-30T15:17:28.889Z",
